  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Report door (#1696, PR #1798) puts the Debug info report into the GitHub new-issue URL. The \"Project:\" line of that report had the full path of the project file. That path usually has the user name in it, and the browser sends it to github.com.\n\n- `debug_info::shared_report` is a new form of the same report. It gives the project file and the machine file by file name only. If the status line has the exact project path (for example after a save), it shows the file name in its place.\n- `report::report_body` uses `shared_report`. The Report door URL thus has no directory part of the project path.\n- `debug_info::report` (the Debug info panel in the application) keeps the full paths. It stays on the machine.\n- An unsaved project still reads `Project: unsaved`. A path with no file name part reads `(no file name)`.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2744-report-door-file-name.md`.\n\nNo label, layout or window changes. No structural assertion changes. No snapshot PNG changes. Screenshots are not necessary, because the PR changes no layout.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Pinning test, alone: `ui lib ::the_report_door_url_has_the_project_file_name_and_no_directory` ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head `e6565e1fd`: 9 steps, 0 failed (ui build, ui lib, boundary, boundary_picks, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files, waterjet_tool).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `report_tests::the_report_door_url_has_the_project_file_name_and_no_directory` (new). It sets a project path in a user home directory (`C:\\Users\\jane.doe\\Parts` on Windows, `/home/jane.doe/Parts` on other systems) and a status line with that path. It asserts that the body and the URL have `Project: bracket.camproj`, and that no directory part is in the body or in the URL, as typed or percent-encoded. It also asserts that the in-app report keeps the full path.\n- `report_tests::the_body_carries_the_questions_and_the_debug_report` (changed). It now embeds `shared_report` and asserts `Project: unsaved` for an unsaved project.\n- The other `report_tests` and `debug_info_tests` are unchanged and green in the ui lib step.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real browser and GitHub. The test checks the URL that the door builds, not the page that GitHub opens.\n- Linux and macOS path forms ran only through the `cfg!` branch of the test, not on those systems.\n- Free text in the status line that has a path other than the exact project path (for example an export path). The shared form does not scrub it.\n\nChangelog: The Report door now sends only the file name of the project and the machine file to GitHub, not the full path on your disk.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2744\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
